; Anomaly Coop - F3a multilevel, docs\SPLIT_LEVELS.md section 4: the domain `level`. What an object online on a level does runs on
; the process that computes that level: the host's process for its level and, with split levels, a map server for each other. Everything else
; of the world stays `host`: sim_board, smart_terrain, sim_squad_*, tasks_*, warfare*, xr_effects, xr_conditions, the story.
;
; These sections are no routes: a route says where a handler runs with one level for everybody, and the generated
; coop_route_stock.ltx / coop_route_gamma.ltx stay as they are. These lines name, among what runs on the host, what is the behaviour
; of an online object (xrCoop\coop_routes.h Table::level_behaviour). With coop_split_levels off nothing changes: `level` then runs
; exactly where `host` does.

